# Service layer is required

Noche Live is a Rails app. Use-case logic belongs in `app/services`, not in controllers and not as orchestrating class methods on ActiveRecord models.

```text
Controller  →  auth, params, one Service.call, respond
Service     →  transaction, locks, idempotency, scoring, broadcast
Model       →  associations, validations, scopes, predicates, single-row state
```

## Do

- Add `app/services/<namespace>/<verb>.rb` → `Namespace::Verb` with `.call(**kwargs)`.
- One class, one use case (`Buzzes::Accept`, `Answers::Submit`, `Scores::Apply`, `Nights::Broadcast`, `Rounds::Open`).
- When you touch a use case still living on a model or controller, extract it in the same change.
- Test use cases in `test/services/`.

## Do not

- Put scoring, locking, multi-model writes, auto-grading, or broadcasts in a controller.
- Add `Model.accept!` / `submit!` / `tap!` / `start!` orchestration on ActiveRecord.
- Leave POROs in `app/models` (`ScoreApplier`, `NightBroadcaster` belong in services).
- Invent a `GameEngine` god object or a Result monad.
- Skip a service because the prompt also says "prefer fewer abstractions". That exception does not apply here.
